        "symbol": "MU",
        "action": "hold",
        "summary": "No position exists, so hold is the only valid action. The fresh 902.78/903.08 quote (2026-10-19 18:32 UTC) shows the intraday bounce fading — from the 878.84 Oct 16 close the stock rallied through ~919 earlier today and has now given back most of that, consistent with an unconfirmed counter-trend move against a -13.5% twenty-session decline. New pricing resolves only pricing objections; the two blocking economic gates from the prior holds are untouched: no certified mid-cycle EPS anchor net of the $5,968M Singapore tax benefit and the 53rd week, and floor-margin durability remains management assertion. Buying today would be a headline-to-buy shortcut.",
        "thesis": "MU remains a research/watch file with no position. Verified primary facts stand: FY2026 revenue $133,188M, gross margin 81% driven by ASP increases, diluted EPS $74.33, noncurrent customer contract liabilities $12,895M versus $142M a year earlier, long-term debt cut to $4,688M (6e74648947d1b765). The 10-K take-or-pay language is read directly: contractually enforceable volumes, minimum/maximum price bands, deposits and letters of credit, with management asserting floor pricing would still yield margins above any prior peak quarter (7bf4ba22c6915e70) — but that floor claim is issuer assertion, and the risk factors concede ASP swings of roughly +200% to -50% and customers having overstated demand (7d7bd87aba354174, 6d6f0938e43acd08). Today's tape is two-sided: a ~3% bounce on Dell/analyst headlines and NVHBM standardization reports (b60b8c80543e31b4, 3988e8d22f88138e), none independently verified, against RSI 33.2, MACD histogram -23.9, price below SMA20/50 and Bollinger mid-band, and 48% annualized volatility (9cfb04e621279385). At ~903 the trailing multiple is roughly 12x peak-cycle EPS — cheap only if FY2026 is not the ceiling, with DGS30 at 5.43% keeping discount rates punitive. The Q1 FY2027 report in late December (gross margin versus 81%, ASP direction, RPO/contract-liability trend) remains the catalyst that can settle the trough-floor dispute.",
        "countercase": "The strongest case against holding: the entry gate has narrowed materially — enforceable take-or-pay bands, $134B RPO, $13B contract liabilities and customer diversification are now read from primary filing pages; Monday's memory-complex breadth (SK hynix +5%, Sandisk +6%, Micron +3%) suggests the CXMT sell-off is being discounted; and shortage commentary points into 2027. Waiting for December could surrender a structural re-rating. Counters: every bullish datapoint today is single-publisher and unverified; the bounce has already faded from ~919 to ~903 within hours, which is the behavior of a capitulation rebound, not a base; insider Form 4s filed 2026-10-15 have unreviewed footnotes; and a 5.43% 30-year with HY spreads grinding wider is a regime no one-day bounce overcomes. Without a mid-cycle EPS anchor, 0.5% sizing would be arbitrary precisely where the peak-cycle-trap downside is least forgiving.",
        "invalidation": "This hold converts to a directional candidate only when: (1) a certified mid-cycle EPS reference net of the $5,968M Singapore tax benefit and the 53rd week is benchmarked against enforceable band floors, defining entry valuation, 0.5% sizing and a 2-ATR stop (~92.5 at ATR14 46.26); or (2) Q1 FY2027 results confirm gross margin near 81%, stable ASPs and RPO/contract-liability growth. Downgrade triggers flip the file bearish: certified review finding unenforceable or concentrated band terms or renegotiation rights; confirmed Q1 FY2027 margin or ASP deterioration versus the 81%/$74.33 anchor; or HY spreads sustaining above ~3.5-3.6% with continued breadth losses while the 10-year stays above ~4.9%. A single headline-driven session in either direction — including today's bounce and fade — is explicitly not a trigger.",
